= "A word for the press, mister President?"

It is custom for the newly elected Prime Minister to deliver an inaugural address marking the start of their term and, by extension, the new parliamentary session. Until now, these speeches have consistently reflected Earth's colonial dominion over our planet; indeed, if there is one trait utterly foreign to the PEC, it is charisma. We now have a golden opportunity to reshape the public's relationship with the premiership, and if there is one thing our entire party agrees on, it is that this chance must not be wasted.

- @first_line_coalition: "I want to start this adress by thanking the new cabinet..."
- @first_line_party: "I want to start this adress by thanking the SPM leadership..."
- @first_line_people: "I want to start this adress by thanking fellow Marsians..."

